First Author: Ayer
Title: A Novel Model to Predict Progression to Death After Withdrawal of Care in Potential Donation-After-Circulatory-Death Heart Donors
Source number: 60

Very short summary: This retrospective US study developed prediction models using 234 consecutive potential donation-after-circulatory-death heart-donor offers and externally validated the selected model in 53 offers from a distant centre. Four supervised machine-learning algorithms were compared with multivariate logistic regression; logistic regression was selected as the final model and achieved an external-validation AUC of 0.88, sensitivity of 100%, specificity of 50%, PPV of 64%, and NPV of 100%.

