	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The study compared multivariate logistic regression with random forest, decision tree, radial-basis-function SVM, and Gaussian naïve Bayes. Candidate predictors were first identified by significant univariate logistic-regression associations, followed by backward elimination for the multivariable logistic model. Five-fold stratified cross-validation was used for candidate-model comparison, after which the selected logistic-regression model was trained on the full development cohort and externally validated at New York University. Interpretability was explicit: the authors preferred logistic regression partly because of its “greater interpretability,” and Table 4 provides model coefficients. No hyperparameter-search procedure was reported for the four machine-learning algorithms.

